0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-container-image-is-not","title":["What ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," is not"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-actual-model","title":"The actual model"},{"depth":2,"url":"#build-a-worker-image","title":"Build a worker image"},{"depth":2,"url":"#wire-up-the-routing","title":"Wire up the routing"},{"depth":3,"url":"#declare-the-key-on-the-scheduler","title":"Declare the key on the scheduler"},{"depth":3,"url":"#advertise-it-on-each-worker","title":"Advertise it on each worker"},{"depth":3,"url":"#request-it-from-the-build","title":"Request it from the build"},{"depth":2,"url":"#rolling-an-image-without-stranding-actions","title":"Rolling an image without stranding actions"},{"depth":2,"url":"#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting"},{"depth":2,"url":"#faq","title":"FAQ"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Containers and images"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"What the container-image property actually does (and doesn't), plus how to build worker images and keep what your build requests in sync with what your fleet advertises."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone whose actions need a specific environment, and\nanyone running more than one kind of worker image. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the\nend:"}]," worker images that carry your toolchain, and a routing scheme that\nsends each action to the right one. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," twenty minutes."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A cache serving hits to your build. If you don't have one yet, start with ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started","children":"Getting started"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-container-image-is-not","children":["What ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," is not"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Start here, because the name is misleading and the misunderstanding is\nexpensive."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Forge does not pull an image and launch a container for each action."}],"\nNo code sits behind the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," key. Search the source for it\nand you will find it in example configs, in the LRE platform definitions under\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"local-remote-execution/"}],", and in CI wiring; nothing in the scheduler or worker\nsource reads it. It is an ordinary string platform property with an evocative\nname."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["What it actually expresses is: ",["$","em",null,{"children":"this worker process is running inside this\nimage"}],". The worker asserts a value, the build requests a value, and the\nscheduler matches them like any other ",["$","code",null,{"children":"exact"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"priority"}]," property. The\nenvironment is real; it's just established by how you ",["$","em",null,{"children":"started the worker"}],",\nnot by anything the scheduler does per action."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":