8:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"Byte-for-byte or nothing"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The repo's own CI action puts it plainly: the value you request \"must\nbyte-for-byte match the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," the claim's worker pool\nadvertises, or actions queue forever.\" No normalisation, no tag\nresolution, no digest comparison. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"debian:bookworm-slim"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"docker.io/library/debian:bookworm-slim"}]," are different strings and\ntherefore different pools."]}]]}]
9:["$","p",null,{"children":["That failure is the silent-queue failure from\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"Platform properties"}],", and it is by\nfar the most common way a container-image scheme goes wrong."]}]
