b:["$","$L32",null,{"children":"flowchart LR\n  I[\"base image<br/>(your toolchain)\"] -->|createWorker| WI[\"forge-worker-*<br/>image\"]\n  WI -->|\"docker run / k8s pod\"| WP[\"worker process<br/>advertises container-image\"]\n  WP -->|connect_worker| S[scheduler]\n  A[\"action<br/>requests container-image\"] --> S\n  S -->|match| WP"}]
c:["$","p",null,{"children":["One image per worker ",["$","em",null,{"children":"pool"}],". Every action a given worker runs shares that\nworker's environment. Heterogeneity comes from running several pools and\nrouting between them, not from varying the image per action."]}]
d:["$","p",null,{"children":["This has a consequence worth planning around: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"image churn is a fleet\noperation."}]," Changing a toolchain means building a new image, rolling a pool\nonto it, and changing what builds request, in an order that doesn't strand\nactions in the queue. There's a safe sequence below."]}]
