22:["$","$L3e",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L3f",null,{"title":"Can a single worker serve multiple images?","id":"can-a-single-worker-serve-multiple-images","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Not meaningfully. A worker process runs in one environment; the property is\nan assertion about that environment. You can advertise several values for a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"priority"}]," key, but that's a routing label, not a second toolchain. Run one\npool per image."]}]}],["$","$L3f",null,{"title":"What if I want a real container per action?","id":"what-if-i-want-a-real-container-per-action","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["The worker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"entrypoint"}]," option lets you interpose a wrapper: the configured\nprogram is prepended to every action's command line as its first argument\n(the config comment says \"command + arguments\", but the code prepends the\nstring as a single program path, so point it at one executable and let that\nexecutable take the action's command as its arguments), which makes a script\nthat launches a container and forwards the command possible. If that wrapper\nenforces its own timeouts, set\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"timeout_handled_externally"}]," so Forge doesn't also time the action out.\nThis is a real deployment shape, but it is something you build, not something\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," gives you."]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-config/src/cas_server.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-config/src/cas_server.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-config/src/cas_server.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"LocalWorkerConfig"]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"inner_execute"]}]]}],["$","$L3f",null,{"title":"Do I need containers at all?","id":"do-i-need-containers-at-all","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["No. Workers run fine as plain processes on bare metal or a VM; the property\nis only a matching string, so a fleet that doesn't use containers\ndoesn't declare the key.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/deploy-bare-metal","children":"Deploy on bare metal"}]," covers that shape."]}]}],["$","$L3f",null,{"title":"How does this relate to LRE?","id":"how-does-this-relate-to-lre","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["They're the two answers to the same question. Images make the ",["$","em",null,{"children":"fleet"}],"\nreproducible: every action in a pool sees the same environment.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/toolchains-and-hermeticity","children":"LRE"}]," makes the ","$L40","\nreproducible by pinning the toolchain into the action itself, which\nadditionally lets a developer's laptop share cache entries with the fleet.\nThey compose: the ","$L41"," and ","$L42"," workers are container images whose\ncontents are Nix-pinned."]}]}],"$L43"]}]
